<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Shichong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 621</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Shichong was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> general who held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> during the dynasty's collapse. In 619 he deposed the Sui emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-tong">Yang Tong</a> and proclaimed his own state of Zheng. Besieged by the Tang under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a>, he lost his ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dou-jiande">Dou Jiande</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hulao">Battle of Hulao</a> in 621 and surrendered; he was murdered on his way into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-shichong.jpg" alt="Wang Shichong" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%8E%8B%E4%B8%96%E5%85%85%EF%BC%88%E8%AA%AA%E5%94%90%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E5%85%A8%E5%82%B3%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
